Next, consider the size of $f'(h)$.
Each strongly connected edge set corresponds to a specific tree shape below a given node $n \in V(T_1) \cup V(T_2)$.
In the worst case, the considered region below the given node is a complete $d$-ary tree, meaning that any tree $d$-ary tree shape is possible.
Thus, in the worst case, $f'$ describes the number of $d$-ary trees of depth $h$, where $d = \max(\deg(T_1),\deg(T_2))$.
To the best of our knowledge, there is no closed form for this function.

