its OOBE by $10$ dB\footnote{See FCC's DA 25-197}, despite formal objections from terrestrial operators, including AT\&T and Verizon, and from EchoStar. The waiver stipulated that Starlink must continue to adhere to strict OOBE limits and engage in active interference resolution with affected parties. 
