In \BSA, we denote the spiking activations  at time step $t$ in layer $l$, token $n$, and input feature dimension $d$ by $X^{(l)}_{n,t,d}$, and a bundle for layer $l$  by $TTB^{(l)}_{bn, bt, d}$, where $bn$, $bt$, and $d$ are the bundle-token, bundle-time, and input feature index, respectively. While $TTB^{(l)}_{bn, bt, d}$ packs multiple tokens and time steps, its activity tag  $Z_{bn,bt,d}$  is defined by the  $L_{0}$ norm of the spiking activations  that fall within it: 
%and the corresponding sets of packed tokens and time points are  denoted by ${\Omega}_{bn}$ and ${\Omega}_{bt}$, respectively. 

