Table \ref{table:pressureHVACs} indicates that DPSs have a sampling frequency of 0.5-2 kHz. However, at least 8 kHz sampling is required to recover intelligible speech. Therefore, a natural question is: \textit{Will it be possible to capture intelligible speech with at least 0.5 kHz sampling frequency using pressure sensors?}. The pitch frequencies for a male speaker vary between 85-180 Hz, whereas for a female speaker, they vary between 165-255 Hz \cite{kent1997speech}. Although the 0.5 kHz sampling rate can capture pitches and a few harmonics,  it is not sufficient to provide perfect intelligibility \cite{fant1960acoustic}, as most harmonics at high frequencies will be missing from the bandwidth. 

