%$\ell_1$-, $\ell_2$-, and other norms. 

%\footnote{There are other important parameters, such as the preprocessing time. For simplicity, we will focus on the query time and space.}

In the so-called {\em low-dimensional regime} \cite{AndoniNNRW17}---when $d=o(\log n)$ and thus the data structure's space and time complexities can be {\em exponential} in $d$---classical data structures can solve this problem efficiently (e.g. \cite{DBLP:journals/dcg/Clarkson99, DBLP:conf/stoc/KargerR02, DBLP:conf/soda/KrauthgamerL04, DBLP:conf/icml/BeygelzimerKL06}). Recently, novel techniques such as locality-sensitive hashing and sketching (e.g. \cite{DBLP:conf/stoc/IndykM98, DBLP:journals/cacm/AndoniI08, DBLP:conf/soda/AndoniINR14, DBLP:conf/stoc/AndoniR15, indyk-wagner18:apx-nn-limited-space}) have led to a new wave of data structures in the {\em high-dimensional regime} 
