In contrast to other regimes, where many efficient $(1+\epsilon)$-approximation data structures are known, no  $(1+\epsilon)$-approximation data structure is known for the ultra-high dimensional regime for any norm, and even when we allow higher space and query time (e.g. $\poly(n)\cdot o(d)$ space and query time).


