\paragraph{Analysis.}  Let $q'$ be a truncated point where $q'^{(i)} = \trunc_{\{l^{(i)}, u^{(i)}\}}(q^{(i)})$, $ \forall i\in [d]$.  

We can bound the random variables:
    $0 \leq X_t, Y_t \leq (1+1/\epsilon)^p$ because 
    \begin{equation}\label{eq:rv-bound}
        0 \leq X_t \leq (1+\frac{1}{(1+\epsilon)^{p/(p-1)}-1})^p \leq (1+\frac{1}{(1+\epsilon(p/(p-1))-1})^p = (1+\frac{p-1}{p\epsilon})^p \leq (1+1/\epsilon)^{p}.          
