\begin{defn}
   A (possibly large) (lex) site is \textit{Morita-small} if it is Morita equivalent to a small (lex) site. This gives us $\mathsf{SITES}_{\mathsf{M}}$, the full sub $2$-category of Morita-small sites.   An algebra $\mc C$ for $\mathsf{T}^{\Hcal}$ is \textit{Morita-small} if the resulting site is Morita-small. Morita-small algebras are collected in the $2$-category $\mathsf{Alg}(\mathsf{T}^{\Hcal})_{\mathsf{M}}$.
\end{defn}


