the schema and contextual details of the table (cf.\ \autoref{fig1}-(e) and Section~\ref{sec:prompt-construction}). This prompt is then passed to a Gen-LLM to generate an ontology fragment specific to the current table, referred to as the \textit{delta-ontology} (\autoref{fig1}-(f)).

Before integrating this delta-ontology into the continuously expanding core ontology (\autoref{fig1}-(h) and cf. Section~\ref{sec:integration}), it undergoes verification and refinement, either automatically (via a \textit{judge-LLM}) or manually by a domain expert (cf. Section~\ref{sec:validation-refinement}, \autoref{fig1}-(f)). 
This ensures semantic consistency and correctness of the generated ontology fragments.

