\subsection{Iterative Integration and Completion}
\label{sec:integration}
After each cycle, the verified delta ontology $\Delta\mathcal{O}_r$ is merged into the core ontology $\mathcal{O}_t$ to form $\mathcal{O}_{t+1}$ (\autoref{fig:promptbox}-(h)).  
New classes, attributes, and axioms enlarge the core ontology while preserving external IRI references and reconciling duplicate concepts.  
The pipeline then follows foreign-key links to the next table, repeating the process until all tables, columns, and relationships have been covered. 
% \steffen{The notion of `foreign-key semantics' is doubtful. Foreign keys are a constraint. The elements in one column (or a set of columns) must be contained in another set.}
The result is a complete OWL~2~DL ontology that mirrors the entire relational schema links entities via foreign-key constraints and incorporates external domain knowledge to meet ontology best-practice standards.

