\subsection{Competency Question Generation} \label{CQ_GEN}
We use CQs to evaluate the quality of the generated ontologies. CQs were generated using \texttt{Mistral-Small-24B-Instruct-2501} and verified by a domain expert. CQs are formulated as natural language questions and corresponding answers that reflect the type of information a specific SQL query is capable of retrieving. In our experiments, the Mistral model outperformed ChatGPT in generating high-quality CQs, as supported by prior comparative evaluations \cite{kommineni2024humanexpertsmachinesllm}. The superior performance of Mistral in this task highlights its suitability for structured-query-driven ontology validation and question-answering scenarios. We used the chain-of-thought prompt engineering technique \cite{DBLP:conf/nips/Wei0SBIXCLZ22} to generate these CQs, as shown in Appendix \ref{box:prompt-example}, Figure \ref{cq_generation_prompt}. 


