Finally, the AO-based algorithm, summarized in \textbf{Algorithm \ref{algorithm1}}, is proposed to solve ${\mathcal{P}_0}$ through combining four subproblems discussed, where $\varepsilon $ denotes the tolerance of convergence and 
$E\left( {{\mathbf A}^{\left( m \right)},{\mathbf B}^{\left( m \right)},{{\mathbf {\tilde{W}}}^{\left( m \right)}},{\mathbf Q}_s^{\left( m \right)}} \right)$ denotes the objective function of the original problem at the $m$-th iteration. }


